content":"Reserved and unused ping/pong forms do not establish a session. Reply and Eviction are client-bound and rejected on replica ingress. A replica Request uses the internal routed-request header, including its group and metadata watermark."},"334":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-111","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#consensus-and-history","content":"The metadata group orders resources, users and sessions. Every partition has its own group for messages and offsets. The group field identifies the target. The metadata group uses 1 << 63, while partition groups use packed stream, topic and partition IDs."},"335":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-112","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#consensus-and-history","content":"Prepare carries an operation and its body. PrepareOk acknowledges the required replication and persistence work. Commit broadcasts the commit point and a liveness token. CommitReply proves that peers still respond. A primary that cannot reach a quorum relinquishes leadership."},"336":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-113","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#consensus-and-history","content":"StartViewChange, DoViewChange and StartView establish a new view. DoViewChange includes an untrusted-log flag so a replica without proven history cannot vote as an authoritative empty log. RequestStartView probes for the current view after recovery."},"337":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-114","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#consensus-and-history","content":"Partition incarnation fields fence an old partition history. Consumer ownership generations separately fence old group members. PrimaryRebalance moves a partition primary under metadata coordination. PrepareProgress lets a 