"tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"RequestPrepares asks for a retained operation range. RepairPrepare sends the original prepares. RepairDone terminates the stream, and RangeEvicted reports history that is no longer retained. Requests are bounded by repair_chunk_max and the peer queue capacity."},"785":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-562","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"State transfer handles larger gaps. RequestStateTransfer obtains a manifest, then RequestStateChunk and StateChunk transfer artifacts. The receiver checks each complete artifact against its manifest length and checksum before using it. The manifest has magic ISM1, a u32 entry count, a u8 entry length and a trailing XxHash3-64 checksum. Entries contain kind, frontier, length and checksum."},"786":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-563","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"Kind"},"787":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-564","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"Artifact"},"788":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-565","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"Current format"},"789":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-566","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"0"},"790":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-567","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster#repair-and-state-transfer","content":"Metadata snapshot"},"791":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/cluster-568","pag