n and close that link. 8 (Reply) continues."},"1387":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-351","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"Read the remaining size - 256 body bytes."},"1388":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-352","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"If status is nonzero, this reply reports a pre-commit rejection. It does not settle an earlier uncertain attempt. The body is empty."},"1389":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-353","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#replyheader","content":"Decode the body and any result section. To settle an uncertain mutation, also require the committed-result marker and matching original request identity."},"1390":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-354","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"Replies for all metadata operations, including their server-internal rewrites, and for the partition-plane consumer-offset writes (StoreConsumerOffset, DeleteConsumerOffset) are result-framed. Non-empty Register replies use the same framing. The body starts with a result section ahead of the typed payload."},"1391":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-355","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"Success: count = 0, and the typed response payload (if any) follows the 4 count bytes."},"1392":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-356","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"Business or transient rejection: one entry { index: 0, result: error_code } and no payload."},"1393":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-357","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"A nonzero header status has an empty body. With status = 0, decode the result section for the operations above: it can report either a committed outcome or a pre-commit transient rejection. Its presence alone does not prove commitment. A matching final result also needs the committed-result marker at byte 220. Replayed PAT creation cannot return the original secret and can report PersonalAccessTokenAlreadyExists with that proof. A successful login-register reply starts with count = 0, followed by the login response payload. An empty Register body is a terminal failure, not a successful login."},"1394":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-358","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#result-section","content":"Replies to non-replicated commands aren't result-framed: after status = 0 the body is the response payload directly."},"1395":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-359","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#evictionheader","content":"Server to client. 256 bytes, never a body. An eviction has no per-request correlation. Close the affected link. A stale-client eviction can occur while the logical session is still live, so try binding the retained session before replacing it. A terminal bind refusal requires a new registration."},"1396":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-360","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#evictionheader","content":"Offset"},"1397":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-361","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing#evictionheader","content":"Size"},"1398":{"id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing-362","page_id":"/docs/binary-protocol/framing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bi