":"/docs/cli/commands-24","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands","content":"This page lists every top-level iggy command. Examples assume you're already authenticated, for example via iggy login. See installation and authentication. Run iggy <command> --help for the full flag list of any command."},"1683":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-25","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands","content":"Conventions used throughout:"},"1684":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-26","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands","content":"Commands that address an existing stream, topic, user, or consumer group accept its numeric ID or name (for example, iggy topic get dev events). Numeric IDs identify the same resources only when those are the IDs assigned by the server. The numeric stream/topic IDs inside permission specifications are an exception: names are not accepted there."},"1685":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-27","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands","content":"Subcommands have single-letter aliases too: c (create), d (delete), g (get), l (list), u (update). So iggy s l is iggy stream list."},"1686":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-28","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands","content":"Every list command accepts -l, --list-mode <table|list> (default: table)."},"1687":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-29","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands","content":"-q, --quiet suppresses ordinary status output. stats still prints its result, and pat create still prints an unstored token. Interactive password changes also print their confirmation. -d, --debug <file> writes verbose logs to a file."},"1688":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-30","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#stream","content":"Manage streams, the top-level containers for topics. Subcommands: create, delete, update, get, list. The legacy creation flags stream create -s, topic create -t, and consumer-group create -g are accepted but ignored. IDs are always assigned by the server."},"1689":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-31","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Manage topics within a stream. Subcommands: create, delete, update, get, list. These examples require an existing dev stream."},"1690":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-32","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Compression is a required positional: none or gzip. It is stored as topic metadata, but compression is not applied. Expiry is a human-readable duration (7d, 1day 12h, unlimited). Omitting expiry at creation selects no expiration."},"1691":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-33","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"For updates, supply expiry and --max-topic-size explicitly. Omitted values are sent as server_default (zero): the server retains the previous expiry/size fields but reports zero in their option entries. See Topic options for this inconsistency."},"1692":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-34","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Flag"},"1693":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-35","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Description"},"1694":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-36","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"-t, --topic-id <ID>"},"1695":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-37","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Accepted at creation but ignored. The server assigns the ID"},"1696":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-38","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"-m, --max-topic-size <SIZE>"},"1697":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-39","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Retention size, e.g. 15GB, unlimited (default: server_default. Unlimited at creation)"},"1698":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-40","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"--durability <POLICY>"},"1699":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-41","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Message completion policy: replicated (default) or persisted (create only)"},"1700":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-42","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"--consumer-offset-durability <POLICY>"},"1701":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-43","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Independent offset-store/delete policy: replicated (default) or persisted (create only)"},"1702":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-44","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"--set <KEY=VALUE>"},"1703":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-45","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#topic","content":"Server-side option, repeatable. Updates accept only updatable keys."},"1704":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-46","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#partition","content":"Add or remove partitions of a topic."},"1705":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-47","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#segment","content":"Delete up to the requested number of oldest sealed segments of a partition. The active segment is retained."},"1706":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-48","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message","content":"Send and poll messages. Subcommands: send and poll. The flush command is removed."},"1707":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-49","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"Flag"},"1708":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-50","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"Description"},"1709":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-51","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"-p, --partition-id <ID>"},"1710":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-52","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"Send to a specific partition"},"1711":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-53","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"-m, --message-key <KEY>"},"1712":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-54","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"Route by a 1-255 byte message key. Binary transports hash it client-side. HTTP resolves it server-side. Mutually exclusive with --partition-id"},"1713":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-55","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"-H, --headers <KEY:KIND:VALUE>"},"1714":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-56","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"Message headers, comma separated. Kinds: raw, string, bool, int8-int128, uint8-uint128, float32, float64"},"1715":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-57","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"--input-file <FILE>"},"1716":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-58","page_id":"/docs/cli/commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli/commands#message-send","content":"Send messages from a binary file written by poll --output-file"},"1717":{"id":"/docs/cli/commands-59","p