ce archive. Swift uses the root Swift Package Manager manifest. See Upgrading before replacing an existing deployment."},"3365":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-96","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#prerequisites","content":"The examples below use the iggy/iggy root credentials. For a new local development instance, with no IGGY_ROOT_USERNAME or IGGY_ROOT_PASSWORD overrides, use:"},"3366":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-97","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#prerequisites","content":"--fresh wipes this replica's local data directory. In a cluster, it can recover stored credentials from another replica. The environment takes precedence over the default-credentials flag, and bootstrap settings do not replace recovered credentials. This setup is for development only. Use a disposable data directory. See Connection Strings for the authentication details."},"3367":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-98","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Every SDK has connection-string support. Accepted schemes, credentials and options differ by language. Java currently accepts username/password TCP strings with tls and tls_ca_file only. They provide a compact way to configure the client, including the transport protocol, credentials, server address, and options."},"3368":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-99","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Format:"},"3369":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-100","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Transport selection via scheme:"},"3370":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-101","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Scheme"},"3371":{"id":"/docs