ntroduction#polling-strategies","content":"next()"},"3410":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-141","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#polling-strategies","content":"Continue after the stored consumer offset, or start at zero if none is stored"},"3411":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-142","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"When sending messages, you can control partition routing (Rust method names are shown):"},"3412":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-143","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"Strategy"},"3413":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-144","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"Description"},"3414":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-145","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"partition_id(n)"},"3415":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-146","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"Send to a specific partition"},"3416":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-147","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"balanced()"},"3417":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-148","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"Round-robin across partitions"},"3418":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-149","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"messages_key(key)"},"3419":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-150","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"Hash-based routing by key"},"3420":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-151","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#partitioning-strategies","content":"The Rust SDK resolves these strategies before sending a binary request. The HTTP API can resolve the strategy on the server. Binary clients route to the selected partition primary."},"3421":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-152","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#read-and-recovery-apis","content":"Use deferred polling to wait for messages. A partition reader groups partitions by primary, and a consumer hands messages to the application one at a time. PollOptions defines the count, wait, byte budget and commit policy. Manual commits are the shared default."},"3422":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-153","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#read-and-recovery-apis","content":"Resource creation accepts typed options. Updates use patches that change only supplied fields and can reset supported defaults. See Topic options and Stream options."},"3423":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-154","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#read-and-recovery-apis","content":"SDKs also expose metadata changes and raw requests to a selected replica. Recovery APIs differ. Swift does not expose retained mutation resolution or pending mutation limits. It has abandonment for uncertain committing reads. Read each language guide before implementing retries after an uncertain write."},"3424":{"id":"/docs/sdk/metadata-changes","page_id":"/docs/sdk/metadata-changes","type":"page","content":"Metadata Changes","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/metadata-changes"},"3425":{"id":"/docs/sdk/metadata-changes-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/metadata-changes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/metadata-changes","content