w"},"3786":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-168","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"\"5 s\""},"3787":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-169","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"Tolerance for clock differences during validation."},"3788":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-170","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"not_before"},"3789":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-171","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"\"0 s\""},"3790":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-172","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"Time before which a token is not valid."},"3791":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-173","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"encoding_secret"},"3792":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-174","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"\"\" (empty)"},"3793":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-175","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"Signing key. If only one secret is configured, it is used for both signing and verification. See the fallback rules below."},"3794":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-176","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"decoding_secret"},"3795":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-177","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"\"\" (empty)"},"3796":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-178","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"Verification key. If both secrets are set, they are used as supplied and must agree for self-issued tokens to verify."},"3797":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-179","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"use_base64_secret"},"3798":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-180","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"false"},"3799":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-181","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"Treat the configured secrets as base64-encoded."},"3800":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-182","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"There is no default secret. When both secrets are empty and cluster authentication supplies no key, each server start mints a random signing key, so issued tokens do not survive a restart and are valid only on the node that issued them. If you configure a secret, set it through the environment (IGGY_HTTP_JWT_ENCODING_SECRET / IGGY_HTTP_JWT_DECODING_SECRET), never commit it, and use a long random value."},"3801":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-183","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"In cluster mode the secret has an extra role: a configured secret, identical on every node, makes bearer tokens valid cluster-wide and activates follower-to-primary HTTP forwarding. When both JWT secrets are empty and cluster.auth is enabled, the JWT key is derived from the cluster PSK. Explicit JWT secrets take precedence. Without either, tokens are node-local and forwarding stays disabled."},"3802":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-184","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"Opt-in trust of external token issuers for application-to-application authentication. With none configured, the listener accepts only self-issued tokens using the configured HMAC algorithm (HS256, HS384, or HS512)."},"3803":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-185","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"issuer, audience, and jwks_url are required per entry. username names the active, non-root Iggy account to which the issuer maps. Provision that account before using its tokens. The old user_id key is rejected."},"3804":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-186","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"Enabling an issuer opens an outbound JWKS fetch that is reachable before a token's signature is verified: a token naming the issuer with an unknown key id can trigger a fetch to jwks_url. The target is fixed (not attacker-chosen), concurrent misses coalesce onto one fetch, and repeats are rate-limited to one outbound request per issuer per short window. The same window bounds how quickly a freshly rotated signing key is picked up."},"3805":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-187","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Key"},"3806":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-188","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Default"},"3807":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-189","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Description"},"3808":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-190","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"enabled"},"3809":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-191","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"true"},"3810":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-192","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Expose Prometheus metrics."},"3811":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-193","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"endpoint"},"3812":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-194","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"\"/metrics\""},"3813":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-195","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Metrics path. Must start with /."},"3814":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-196","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"The metrics route requires authentication: a missing or invalid bearer credential is rejected with 401. Any authenticated user may scrape. There's no extra RBAC rule. Scrapers present a JWT or a personal access token as the bearer:"},"3815":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-197","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httptls","content":"Key"},"3816":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-198","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httptls","content":"Default"},"3817":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-199","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httptls","content":"Description"},"3818":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-200","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"te