,"page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#stored-documents","content":"Every document has a generated _id of stream:topic:partition:message_id and a payload field. The offset is not part of the ID. Payload fields remain nested under payload, so a payload's own _id does not replace the connector's ID. Message headers are not stored."},"6020":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-67","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#stored-documents","content":"json parses the payload and converts it to a BSON value under payload, including objects, arrays and scalars. Invalid JSON or an unsupported BSON conversion rejects the whole chunk before insertion."},"6021":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-68","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#stored-documents","content":"string and its text alias require valid UTF-8 and store a BSON string."},"6022":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-69","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#stored-documents","content":"binary stores BSON Binary with the generic subtype. Use schema = \"raw\" and no payload-changing transform to preserve original bytes."},"6023":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-70","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#stored-documents","content":"Format names are case-insensitive. Formatting happens after stream decoding and transforms, so JSON decoding can change the original bytes."},"6024":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-71","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#stored-documents","content":"With include_metadata = true, documents contain iggy_offset, iggy_timestamp, iggy_stream, iggy_topic and iggy_partition_id. Offsets above the signed 64-bit range use iggy_offset_str instead. Partition IDs use a BSON 32-bit integer when possible and a 64-bit integer otherwise. iggy_checksum is a 64-bit integer when possible and a decimal string otherwise. Message and origin timestamps become BSON datetimes, truncating microseconds to milliseconds. Checksum and origin timestamp flags are independent of include_metadata. _id and payload are always present."},"6025":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-72","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#delivery-semantics","content":"Each polled batch is split into chunks of at most batch_size messages. Chunks are inserted immediately with unordered insert_many. Other documents can succeed when one is rejected. Later chunks are still attempted after a failure, and the last chunk error is returned. There is no accumulation across polls and no transaction covering the batch."},"6026":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-73","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#delivery-semantics","content":"The connector retries transient insert failures up to max_retries total attempts, with linear waits of retry_delay, twice that delay, and so on. An invalid delay silently falls back to 1s. Driver-level retryable writes may add retries independently, according to the URI and MongoDB deployment. Startup has no connector-level retry loop."},"6027":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-74","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#delivery-semantics","content":"An insert error containing only duplicate-key errors (11000) and no write-concern error is treated as success. This covers all unique indexes, not only _id, and does not compare payload contents. Reusing a message ID in one stream/topic/partition preserves the existing document. A conflict on another unique index can also discard a distinct message while runtime reports it processed. Account for this when choosing collection indexes."},"6028":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-75","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#delivery-semantics","content":"The runtime auto-commits while polling, records plugin errors and continues without replaying the failed batch. Earlier or later chunks may already be stored, and a timeout can leave the write outcome uncertain. Duplicate tolerance and retries do not provide an end-to-end at-least-once guarantee."},"6029":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-76","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#transforms","content":"You can apply transforms before writing to MongoDB. Every [transforms.*] section requires enabled = true. See the transforms documentation for details."},"6030":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres","type":"page","content":"Postgres Sink","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sinks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres"},"6031":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres","content":"Store messages from Iggy topics in a PostgreSQL table, with optional table creation and configurable payload storage."},"6032":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres#features","content":"Features"},"6033":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"6034":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgres","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/postgr