ges to the Iggy stream instead, you can implement your own Source connector too :)"},"6389":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","type":"page","content":"Stdout Sink","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sinks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout"},"6390":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","content":"Print messages from Iggy streams to standard output, for debugging and verifying a connector pipeline."},"6391":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"6392":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout#plugin-config-options","content":"Plugin config options"},"6393":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","content":"The stdout sink connector prints messages from Iggy streams to the standard output. This is useful for debugging, development, and verifying that your connector pipeline is working correctly."},"6394":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","content":"The connector emits info-level tracing events through the runtime to stdout. The runtime selects text or JSON with logging.format and filters events with RUST_LOG (default INFO). It logs batch metadata on every invocation. print_payload additionally logs each message's offset and decoded payload. The invocation counter is in memory and resets when the plugin is recreated."},"6395":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/stdout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"