connectors/sinks/surrealdb-60","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"auto, json, text, base64, or binary (alias for base64)"},"6467":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-61","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"include_metadata"},"6468":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-62","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"bool"},"6469":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-63","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"true"},"6470":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-64","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"Store stream/topic/partition/offset/timestamp/schema fields"},"6471":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-65","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"The include_headers, include_checksum, and include_origin_timestamp flags also default to true and work independently of include_metadata. Retry and timeout options are query_timeout (30s per HTTP request), max_retries (3 total write attempts, with 0 raised to 1), retry_delay (100ms), and max_retry_delay (5s). Invalid duration strings log a warning and fall back to 1s. Zero durations are accepted. The maximum delay is raised to the base delay if configured smaller. verbose_logging defaults to false and raises per-poll submission logs from debug to info. See the upstream surrealdb_sink README for the full table."},"6472":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-66","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"Namespace, database and table names must start with an ASCII letter or underscore and contain only ASCII letters, digits and underscores. Endpoint URLs cannot contain credentials, a path beyond /, a query or a fragment. An explicit http:// or https:// scheme takes precedence over use_tls. Payload-format and authentication-scope names are case-insensitive. Unknown values prevent startup."},"6473":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-67","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"With root, namespace or database authentication, startup calls /signin and SQL requests use Basic authentication with the configured scope. Namespace/database users require pre-existing resources and auto_define_table = false. With auth_scope = \"none\", credentials are ignored. The server must permit those unauthenticated operations. Automatic DDL uses IF NOT EXISTS and does not migrate existing definitions. The optional <table>_iggy_offset_idx index is not a uniqueness constraint. define_indexes = true with metadata disabled rejects startup. Without automatic DDL it only logs a warning and skips index creation."},"6474":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-68","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Every submitted record contains id, iggy_message_id, payload and payload_encoding. include_metadata adds iggy_stream, iggy_topic, iggy_partition_id, iggy_offset, iggy_timestamp and iggy_schema. The checksum and origin timestamp have separate flags. iggy_headers appears only when enabled and nonempty."},"6475":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-69","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Iggy message IDs, partition IDs, offsets, timestamps and checksums are stored as strings. Timestamps retain Iggy's microsecond values, not SurrealDB datetime values. Record IDs encode stream/topic UTF-8 bytes as hex, then append partition, offset and the 32-digit hexadecimal message ID. Changing the payload or transforms does not change that identity. Changing any identity component creates a different key."},"6476":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-70","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Payload formatting operates after the runtime decoder and transforms:"},"6477":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-71","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"payload_format"},"6478":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-72","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Stored payload and encoding"},"6479":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-73","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"auto"},"6480":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-74","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"JSON values as json. Text/Proto variants as text. Raw/Avro/FlatBuffer bytes as base64, even when raw bytes contain valid JSON"},"6481":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-75","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"json"},"6482":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-76","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"A JSON value, parsing other payload variants as JSON. Invalid JSON is rejected"},"6483":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-77","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"text"},"6484":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-78","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"A string, decoding other payload bytes as UTF-8. Invalid UTF-8 is rejected"},"6485":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-79","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"base64 / binary"},"6486":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-80","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Base64 of the payload bytes, with payload_encoding = \"base64\""},"6487":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-81","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Non-raw headers are stored as strings, including numbers and booleans. Raw headers use {\"data\":\"AQID\",\"iggy_header_encoding\":\"base64\"}. Payload JSON is sent as SurrealQL values, so destination schema, numeric and other value constraints still apply."},"6488":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-82","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#delivery-semantics","content":"The runtime auto-commits while polling, logs/counts plugin callback failures, and continues without replaying the failed batch. The sink retries transaction-conflict errors, connection/timeouts, and HTTP 408, 429, 500, 502, 503 and 504. Delays use capped exponential backoff with jitter. Retry-After is not used. Connection errors trigger reconnection and repeat sign-in/health/optional DDL. A failed reconnect stops that chunk, and retries plus startup requests can exceed query_timeout in total."},"6489":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-83","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#delivery-semantics","content":"A malformed record is skipped while valid records in its chunk are still submitted. A failed chunk does not stop later chunks, and the last error is returned. The sink checks HTTP and SQL statement statuses. Its own processed counter counts records submitted in successful statements, including records ignored by INSERT IGNORE. Runtime counters instead reflect whether the whole callback succeeded. Neither is a count of newly inserted rows."},"6490":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-84","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#delivery-semantics","content":"SurrealQL INSERT IGNORE preserves existing records with the same ID, including their old payloads. With the SurrealDB 3.1.4 instance above, IGNORE also silently skips unique-index conflicts and field-assertion failures while accepting valid records from the same chunk. These skips return a successful statement and are included in processed counters. This protects repeated writes of the same identities. It does not ensure that a failed batch will be delivered. There is no end-to-end at-least-once guarantee."},"6491":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-85","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#transforms","content":"Transforms can be applied before writing to SurrealDB. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."},"6492":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"page","content":"C++ SDK","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","C++"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro"},"6493":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","content":"The C++ SDK, a CXX bridge over the Rust SDK, and how to build it from source with Bazel."},"6494":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-1","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#building-from-source","content":"Building from source"},"6495":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-2","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"6496":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-3","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#connection-strings","content":"Connection strings"},"6497":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-4","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#helper-types","content":"Helper types"},"6498":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-5","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#current-status","content":"Current status"},"6499":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-6","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#readers-and-recovery","content":"Readers and recovery"},"6500":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-7","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","content":"The Iggy C++ SDK wraps the Rust SDK through a CXX FFI bridge, so it can use all transport protocols (TCP, QUIC, HTTP, WebSocket) via connection strings. The source code is available at github.com/apache/iggy/tree/master/foreign/cpp."},"6501":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-8","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","content":"This SDK isn't published to any package registry. Consume it from the monorepo and build it from source with Bazel."},"6502":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-9","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#building-from-source","content":"The project builds with the Bazel version pinned in .bazelversion (BUILD.bazel / MODULE.bazel). Its Rust bridge uses the Cargo and Rust toolchain provisioned by rules_rust, with a separate target directory in the Bazel output tree. Use a compatible Java runtime for Bazel. The pinned Bazel 9.2.0 requires Java 21 or newer."},"6503":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-10","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#quick-start","content":"The snippet below mirrors the SDK's own end-to-end tests in foreign/cpp/tests/e2e. Start a local server on 127.0.0.1:8090 with the iggy/iggy credentials first. The stream name must not already exist."},"6504":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-11","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#quick-start","content":"Polling strategies are selected by kind string: offset, timestamp, first, last, or next. Partitioning kinds for sending are balanced, partition_id, and messages_key."},"6505":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-12","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#connection-strings","content":"The C++ SDK supports the same connection string format as the Rust SDK:"},"6506":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-13","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#connection-strings","content":"iggy::ffi::from_connection_string() accepts these strings. new_connection() instead takes an IggyClientConfig: {} selects TCP at 127.0.0.1:8090 without automatic login, and its server_address field overrides that address. Binary clients authenticate from their connection string during connect(). HTTP requires an explicit login_user() call. See connection strings for the supported options and credential syntax."},"6507":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-14","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#helper-types","content":"Beyond the generated lib.rs.h FFI surface, foreign/cpp/include/iggy.hpp ships typed C++ helpers: CompressionAlgorithm, MaxTopicSize, Expiry, PollingStrategy, IdKind, TopicOption, SnapshotCompression, and SystemSnapshotType, plus the IggyException error type. They construct and validate the kind strings and values the raw FFI calls expect."},"6508":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-15","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#current-status","content":"The FFI bridge exposes command-level operations for streams, topics, partitions, and segments. Message sending and polling with user headers. Consumer groups and consumer offsets. Stats, client info, and cluster metadata. Snapshots. User create/get/update/delete, permission updates and password changes. Topic option discovery (describe_options). And raw binary requests (send_binary_request)."},"6509":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-16","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#current-status","content":"The typed IggyBlockingClient also provides resource management, readers, consumers, offsets, user administration and client inspection. Personal access token creation is exposed by the bridge. Use iggy.hpp for typed StreamCreateOptions, TopicCreateOptions, update patches and PollOptions."},"6510":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-17","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#readers-and-recovery","content":"Reader reads batches from explicit partitions or a group assignment. StandaloneConsumer and GroupConsumer yield individual messages. Call Close before destruction. Manual commits are the default, and reader waits default to five seconds."},"6511":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-18","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#readers-and-recovery","content":"IggyException::OperationId() identifies retained uncertain operations. ResolveOperation retries a mutation with its retained identity, without returning the original payload. AbandonOperation frees local state without undoing the result. A lost committing poll reports fetch_progress_uncertain and blocks partition progress until abandonment."},"6512":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-19","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#readers-and-recovery","content":"The generated bridge passes ErrorInfo by reference to mutations, login, polls and recovery calls. Use a separate value for each concurrent call. GetMetadataChanges follows the metadata log, and send_binary_request_to_replica targets a node for supported non-replicated commands."},"6513":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"page","content":"Examples","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","C#"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples"},"6514":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","content":"Producer and consumer samples for the C# SDK, built on the high-level publisher and consumer."},"6515":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-1","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#producer","content":"Producer"},"6516":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-2","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#consumer-group","content":"Consumer group"},"6517":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-3","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#typed-messages","content":"Typed messages"},"6518":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-4","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#more-examples","content":"More examples"},"6519":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-5","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","content":"These samples use the High-level SDK - the recommended way to build producers and consumers. For the low-level, per-call equivalents, see the Guide."},"6520":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-6","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","content":"Use the installation and server setup first. The snippets share their named resources: run a producer before its corresponding consumer."},"6521":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-7","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#producer","content":"A publisher that creates the stream and topic if missing, batches sends in the background, and retries failures:"},"6522":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-8","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#consumer-group","content":"A consumer that creates and joins a consumer group, stores each offset after handling the yielded message and requesting the next one, and surfaces polling errors:"},"6523":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-9","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#consumer-group","content":"Run several instances of the consumer to see the group load-balance partitions between members."},"6524":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-10","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#typed-messages","content":"A typed publisher/consumer pair that (de)serializes a record as JSON. The typed builders are configured via statements rather than one fluent chain - the With* methods return the untyped base builder, so Build() must be called on the typed builder variable (see Typed consumer):"},"6525":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-11","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#more-examples","content":"The examples/csharp directory in the Iggy repository contains complete, runnable projects:"},"6526":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-12","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#more-examples","content":"Basic / GettingStarted