 of each term, with a link to the page that explains it."],[3246,"A one-shot poll rejects an automatic policy because it has no continuing processing state. On-read commits can precede application processing. A failover before offset replication can also deliver the last batch again. Use manual commits or automatic commits after processing when messages must be processed before their offsets advance."],[2906,"A partition primary orders writes for that partition. Different partitions can have different primaries. replication_factor determines how many nodes store each partition. Metadata has its own primary and spans the full cluster."],[3236,"A partition reader groups targets by their current primary and uses FetchMessages. Each fetch applies count, min_count and max_bytes across its targets together. The reader can keep several fetches active. It can return a partition with messages without waiting for a quiet partition first."],[3026,"A payload can be up to 64 MB, and a message's user headers up to 100 KB in total. The whole send request also has to fit the server's request limit, which by default is 64 MiB over TCP and 2 MB over HTTP."],[6723,"A poll reads one explicit partition. Use a reader for several partitions or a consumer group assignment. PollOptions defaults to no wait and manual commits."],[2071,"A primary orders writes for one consensus group. Iggy has one metadata group and a separate group for each partition. Multi-leader partitions let different nodes lead different partitions at the same time."],[6521,"A publisher that creates the stream and topic if missing, batches sends in the background, and retries failures:"],[2775,"A range (e.g. \"5..8\") - shards on CPUs 5, 6 and 7 when pinning is enabled. Those CPUs must be allowed for the process"],[4126,"a range, e.g. \"5..8\": three shards on cores 5, 6, 7"],[6867,"A read error that stops a partition ends enumeration with ReadException. Inspect StopsPartition, IsResumable and Skip before selecting a new start with SeekAsync. Automatic retries do not discard an undecodable record without an application decision."],[3245,"A reader or consumer tracks progress and stores it by interval or message count"],[3453,"A rebuild reads Current pages, then follows changes from the returned anchor. Keep the rebuilt state private until a change page reports no more records and reaches at least the last current page's head_op. A sequence of current pages alone does not establish that the mirror caught up."],[1263,"A reconnect uses BindSession. Ending the session loses access to unresolved receipts. A fresh operation can duplicate an earlier uncertain write. SDKs retain uncertain operations and block conflicting work until resolution or abandonment."],[3235,"A reply can contain fewer than min_count messages when the wait ends. The first message can exceed max_bytes and return alone, so a large message does not prevent progress. Treat the byte budget as a batching limit, not an absolute allocation guarantee."],[1857,"A request rejected before admission can be retried within its deadline. A lost reply after sending is different: the operation can already be committed. Retained-operation SDKs preserve its original identity and payload instead of submitting a fresh mutation."],[2058,"A restarting replica loads segment and offset state and, when enabled, reconciles the durable prepare WAL with that state. It also restores durable consensus state and follows the recovery protocol before serving as a healthy replica. It does not treat every locally recovered prepare as committed."],[6891,"A retained session can survive transport loss. Reconnect binds it before registering a new session. Logout, session expiry and account deactivation end the session. An uncertain mutation retains its request identity for recovery. Keep the same client and use ResolveOperationAsync or AbandonOperationAsync when an exception reports a retained operation. Abandonment does not undo the server result."],[1261,"A retry keeps the original client, session, request number, logical request stamp and arguments. New mutations use new request numbers. Registration uses request zero. Do not infer that a low-numbered request succeeded because a later request committed."],[5433,"A row that cannot be encoded or accepted is logged and dropped while other rows can proceed. Transient request failures retry with jittered exponential backoff. The _default stream does not provide exactly-once append semantics. A lost response can lead to duplicate rows."],[6908,"A runnable getting-started example lives in the examples/go directory of the core repository. Its go.mod carries a replace directive pointing at the in-repo SDK, so the example always builds against the SDK source in the same checkout. The examples are exercised in CI via scripts/run-examples-from-readme.sh --language go."],[6952,"A runnable getting-started example with producer, consumer, and TLS flags lives in examples/go. See the examples page for how to run it."],[2855,"A SegmentedLog with sealed segments and one active segment"],[4521,"A separate 1 GiB-page experiment requires platform support, a suitable pool, and a budget for each process. mimalloc advises normally choosing this reservation mode separately from MIMALLOC_ALLOW_LARGE_OS_PAGES. See mimalloc environment options. HugeTLB allocation can require CAP_IPC_LOCK or membership in vm.hugetlb_shm_group, as described in mmap permissions."],[1032,"A served partition context is 24 bytes:"],[2055,"A shared barrier can also persist co-batched operations with the weaker policy. That incidental persistence does not strengthen what their earlier replicated acknowledgements promised."],[2441,"A source produces messages to the configured stream and topic. A sink consumes messages from the configured stream(s) and topic(s):"],[2307,"A source that supplies checkpoint bytes gets a file named source_{key}.state (e.g. local_state/source_random.state) holding the raw state bytes - by co