e runtime currently retains only the last producer when multiple entries are supplied."],[4436,"Configure the service"],[7295,"Connect and create resources"],[4566,"Connected clients"],[1782,"Connecting to a server"],[1787,"Connection contexts"],[6543,"Connection events"],[4579,"Connection handling across shards"],[909,"Connection lifecycle"],[1527,"Connection lifecycle: protocol versioning and the login-register handshake."],[6047,"Connection Pooling: Efficient database connection management"],[3120,"Connection receive window size in bytes"],[1063,"Connection rejected, no per-request correlation"],[6875,"Connection semantics"],[6764,"Connection settings - only used when the builder creates its own client (i.e. the Create(streamId, topicId) overload, without an existing client). A builder-created TCP client auto-logs in and reuses the credentials across reconnects. For HTTP, supply an explicitly authenticated client"],[3272,"Connection string"],[3282,"Connection string"],[7142,"Connection string"],[7250,"Connection string"],[2976,"Connection string. A single value such as iggy://user:password@localhost:8090 that tells a client how to connect. All SDKs accept connection strings, with language-specific schemes and options. See Connection strings."],[6496,"Connection strings"],[3027,"Connection Strings"],[7304,"Connection strings accept iggy:// and iggy+tcp://. TLS uses system roots or the configured CA file. tls_domain overrides the name checked in the certificate. The parser accepts pending-operation limits, but does not implement retained mutation limits."],[6932,"Connection strings and metadata"],[5213,"connection_string"],[6056,"connection_string"],[5967,"connection_uri"],[4208,"connections_max"],[5362,"Connector key (String), separate from the numeric plugin instance ID."],[6338,"Connector key (String), separate from the numeric plugin instance ID."],[2387,"Connector runtime has an HTTP API which is enabled by default at 127.0.0.1:8081. It can be disabled by setting the enabled flag to false in the [http] section."],[4993,"Connector sinks use deferred polling. Replace poll_interval with max_wait and min_count. The runtime rejects a sink configuration that still sets poll_interval."],[21,"Connectors"],[2228,"Connectors"],[2645,"Connectors"],[2681,"Connectors - sinks, sources and data transformations based on the custom Rust plugins loaded dynamically at runtime"],[2221,"Connectors are dynamically loaded shared libraries (.so on Linux, .dylib on macOS, .dll on Windows) loaded at runtime via dlopen2. Message batches and metadata crossing the FFI boundary between the runtime and plugins are serialized using postcard, a compact binary format. Plugin configuration is passed as JSON. The SDK initializes one Tokio runtime per loaded plugin library, shared by its connector instances. All plugins run in the same process."],[4343,"Connectors runtime"],[32,"Connectors Runtime - dynamically loaded Rust plugins for data integration: 17 sinks and 6 sources. Ingest from PostgreSQL, Elasticsearch or InfluxDB into Iggy, or forward to MongoDB, Elasticsearch, ClickHouse, Apache Iceberg, Quickwit, S3 and more. Built-in data transforms and Prometheus metrics."],[2140,"Consensus"],[227,"Consensus and history"],[2154,"Consensus group"],[1894,"Consensus runs on a fixed 10ms tick. Every duration below is converted to whole ticks: values are rounded down to a multiple of 10ms, and anything under 10ms is raised to a single tick rather than firing sooner. repair_gap_debounce_interval has an additional 500ms floor."],[1869,"Consensus timing"],[1096,"Consensus view. Send zero."],[4902,"Constraints"],[5753,"Consume messages from Iggy topics and store them in Iceberg tables, with REST catalogs and S3-compatible storage."],[3495,"consume_messages runs until the shutdown event is set. Ctrl-C, or a SIGTERM from a supervisor, sets it, and the current message finishes before the call returns. The instance name is only used in the log."],[7079,"consumeMessages()