ientException, and the IggyException base."],[7056,"Errors: the package exports ResponseError, DeserializeError, ProtocolFrameError, and VsrEvictionError for precise error handling."],[1912,"Escalate a view change that does not conclude within this window to a fresh election"],[3436,"Establish a position at the current end"],[2782,"Event interval: poll the I/O driver after 128 scheduler ticks (roughly task polls) by default"],[1964,"Every address must be routable from inside its own client_cidr: leader-aware clients redial whatever address metadata advertises, and a selector pointing at an unreachable host strands them mid-redirect."],[3665,"Every configuration key can be overridden with an IGGY_ variable. The name is the TOML path, uppercased, with dots turned into underscores:"],[6019,"Every document has a generated _id of stream:topic:partition:message_id and a payload field. The offset is not part of the ID. Payload fields remain nested under payload, so a payload's own _id does not replace the connector's ID. Message headers are not stored."],[1930,"Every duration must be nonzero. The 0, disabled, and unlimited sentinels all parse to a zero duration and are rejected. There's no way to switch the liveness window off."],[339,"Every header begins with the common 128-byte frame prefix shown in Framing. The tables below list the remaining fields in wire order. Multi-byte integers are little-endian. Reserved fields are not extension space for clients. RepairPrepare uses the PrepareHeader layout with its repair command value."],[1658,"Every iggy CLI command with its arguments, flags, and a runnable example"],[1686,"Every list command accepts -l, --list-mode <table|list> (default: table)."],[1043,"Every message on a binary transport is a fixed 256-byte header followed by an optional body. The header is a #[repr(C)] struct decoded by pointer cast (zero-copy), so field offsets are fixed and enforced at compile time in the server. Three header shapes cross the client boundary:"],[1985,"Every node loads the same configuration. Nodes are told apart only by --replica-id, which selects that node's own entry in the cluster.nodes roster."],[2080,"Every node must run the same server version and the same cluster.coordinator.replica_connections_per_peer. There is no rolling upgrade between 0.9 and 0.10. The roster supports at most 32 nodes."],[1966,"Every node must run the same server version. Do not mix 0.9 and 0.10 nodes during an upgrade."],[12,"Every partition is an append-only log. Messages are immutable once written, consumers can start from a chosen offset, and retained messages can be replayed. Retention removes old data, and offsets can contain gaps."],[4609,"Every request and reply on the stateful transports starts with a fixed 256-byte header (the same Viewstamped Replication header layout the cluster uses internally), followed by the command payload. The iggy_binary_protocol crate provides zero-copy serialization for these headers, and foreign SDKs implement the same contract natively. See the Binary Protocol section for the full specification."],[2000,"Every roster field can be provided through typed environment variables instead of TOML, which suits container deployments:"],[3367,"Every SDK has connection-string support. Accepted schemes, credentials and options differ by language. Java currently accepts username/password TCP strings with tls and tls_ca_file only. They provide a compact way to configure the client, including the transport protocol, credentials, server address, and options."],[7199,"Every send method returns a SendMessagesResponse carrying the commit confirmations of the chunks the send was split into. The list is empty whenever the server sends no confirmation payload, and always for a background producer, which hands the messages to a dispatcher and returns before the send happens. Branch on confirmations.is_empty() instead of indexing. A retried chunk may already have been committed by an earlier attempt, so a confirmation offset does not imply uniqueness. Direct-send completion follows the topic's durability policy."],[6474,"Every submitted record contains id, iggy_message_id, payload and payload_encoding. include_metadata adds iggy_stream, iggy_topic, iggy_partition_id, iggy_offset, iggy_timestamp and iggy_schema. The checksum and origin timestamp have separate flags. iggy_headers appears only when enabled and nonempty."],[4183,"evicted_ring_bytes_max"],[4180,"evicted_ring_capacity"],[286,"Eviction"],[1060,"Eviction"],[1468,"Eviction reason, see below."],[1469,"Eviction reasons:"],[1042,"EvictionHeader"],[1046,"EvictionHeader: server to client, connection rejection with no body."],[1369,"Exactly 1 marks a final committed result. Zero and unknown values provide no proof."],[1717,"Exactly one polling strategy is required:"],[2419,"exactly_once=true enables producer batch identity for a source. The plugin must reproduce the same messages from its saved state. The runtime stores producer ID, epoch, sequence and partition with the plugin checkpoint before sending."],[2323,"Exactly-once sources"],[5671,"Example Configurations"],[6513,"Examples"],[6903,"Examples"],[6933,"Examples"],[6953,"Examples"],[6983,"Examples"],[7002,"Examples"],[7032,"Examples"],[7067,"Examples"],[7093,"Examples"],[7111,"Examples"],[7124,"Examples"],[7286,"Examples"],[6902,"Examples - producer, consumer-group, and typed-message samples, plus links to runnable projects"],[7058,"Examples are available in the examples/node directory, written in TypeScript. See Examples for the list and how to run them."],[7005,"Examples are available in the examples/node directory, written in TypeScript. They use the SDK from the same checkout:"],[2203,"Examples are available in the repository for multiple languages: Rust (basic, getting-started, message-envelope, message-headers, multi-tenant, new-sdk, sink-data-producer, stream-builder, tcp-tls), C#, Go, Java, Node.js, PHP, Python and Swift. Docker Compose files and Helm charts are also provided."],[3383,"Examples:"],[2046,"Except for two replicas, the replication quorum is min(ceil(n / 2), 3) and the view-change quorum is n - replication_quorum + 1. Two replicas require both for either quorum. The quorums therefore intersect. These are the implemented quorum rules, not a configurable acknowledgement count."],[5240,"Exclusive starting value when a table has no saved offset"],[2261,"Execute cargo run --example sink-data-producer --release, which sends 100 batches of messages to previously created qw stream and records topic (this will be used by the Quickwit sink connector)."],[1772,"Existing output directory for the snapshot file"],[4302,"Exit if a metadata or partition superblock remains unwritable past this window. \"0\" leaves it fenced indefinitely. Nonzero values must be at least \"30s\"."],[4047,"Expected heartbeat interval."],[3449,"Expired"],[895,"expiry is a duration in microseconds. Two sentinel values exist: 0 (server default, which currently means no expiry) and u64::MAX (never expires)."],[4380,"Explicit consumer-offset stores and deletes"],[4488,"Explicit large pages"],[7210,"Explicit partition IDs. Refused for a group"],[4837,"Explicit stream key"],[2106,"explicitly configured http.jwt signing secrets, identical on every node, or"],[6006,"Explicitly create a missing collection at startup. false still permits creation by the first insert"],[4513,"Explicitly reserved pages. vm.nr_hugepages counts pages of the default size reported by Hugepagesize."],[6809,"Exponential backoff multiplier"],[1988,"Export the settings shared by all three processes:"],[3810,"Expose Prometheus metrics."],[2442,"Expose the implementation with sink_connector!(MySink) or source_connector!(MySource). The sink constructor has the signature new(id: u32, config: MySinkConfig) -> Self. The source constructor also takes state: Option<ConnectorState>. The sink guide and source guide provide complete plugin implementations and build setup."],[3755,"