es, and deletes its resources:"],[6919,"From the repository root, start a disposable server with TLS enabled and the development certificates:"],[2923,"from_connection_string takes the transport, host and credentials in one string, iggy+tcp://user:pass@host:port. See Connection strings for the other options. Creating a stream or topic that already exists is an error, so the producer checks first and only creates what's missing. That's also what makes it safe to run again."],[579,"from_op"],[2664,"Fully operational RESTful API which can be optionally enabled"],[4735,"Further keys (valid_issuers, valid_audiences, not_before, use_base64_secret, the signing secrets) are covered in Configuration."],[6306,"Further options cover credentials (access_key_id / secret_access_key), retries (max_attempts defaults to 3, retry_delay to 1s), and path_style addressing (auto-enabled when endpoint is set, overridable with false). max_retries is an alias for max_attempts. 0 and 1 both make one outer upload attempt. Invalid retry durations prevent startup. 0s is allowed. Output format names are case-insensitive, with jsonl and jsonlines aliases for json_lines. See the upstream s3_sink README for the full reference."],[5711,"Further options cover retries (max_retries, retry_delay, retry_backoff_multiplier, max_retry_delay), success status codes, payload size limits, TLS, connection pooling, health checks, and verbose logging. See the upstream http_sink README for the full list with defaults."],[5943,"Further options cover task polling (task_timeout 30s, task_poll_interval 100ms) and transient retries (max_retries 3, retry_delay 500ms, max_retry_delay 5s, max_open_retries 5). Both retry limits count retries after the first request, so max_retries = 3 permits up to four attempts within the operation deadline. Backoff doubles from retry_delay, adds ±20% jitter and is capped at max_retry_delay. Reversed delay bounds are swapped. Invalid duration strings warn and fall back to 1s. There is no single deadline for the whole startup sequence. See the upstream meilisearch_sink README for details."],[5600,"Further options cover the label prefix, connect timeout, retry backoff (retry_delay, max_retry_delay), max_filter_ratio, a where filter, and redirect security (allow_insecure_redirect, allowed_redirect_hosts). See the upstream doris_sink README for the full table with defaults."],[4556,"gauge"],[4559,"gauge"],[4562,"gauge"],[4565,"gauge"],[5534,"GCS: gcs_service_account_key (the service account JSON as a string, with the bucket taken from the gs:// URI)."],[3990,"Generate a data key for each new stream. Existing streams retain their encryption choice. Payloads and user headers use AES-256-GCM-SIV. Metadata and structural headers are not encrypted as a whole."],[3846,"Generate an ephemeral loopback certificate, but only while cert_file does not exist on disk. An existing PEM pair is loaded instead (the server logs which way it went). false requires both files to exist."],[1841,"Generate completions for bash, zsh, fish, elvish or powershell with --generate:"],[5321,"Generate random messages into Iggy streams for testing, benchmarking and verifying a connector pipeline."],[2390,"GET /: welcome message."],[2391,"GET /health: process liveness response. It does not check connector health. Inspect /stats, /sources or /sinks for connector status."],[2393,"GET /metrics: Prometheus metrics, available when [http.metrics] is enabled (path configurable via its endpoint key)."],[2394,"GET /sinks: list of sinks."],[2395,"GET /sinks/{key}: sink details."],[2396,"GET /sinks/{key}/configs: list of configuration versions for the sink."],[2399,"GET /sinks/{key}/configs/{version}: configuration details for a specific version."],[2400,"GET /sinks/{key}/configs/active: active configuration details."],[2402,"GET /sinks/{key}/configs/plugin: sink plugin config, including the optional format query parameter to specify the config format."],[2403,"GET /sinks/{key}/transforms: sink tra