gy.json:"],[3524,"grafana/provisioning/dashboards/iggy.yaml:"],[3523,"grafana/provisioning/datasources/prometheus.yaml:"],[372,"group"],[417,"group"],[438,"group"],[453,"group"],[468,"group"],[498,"group"],[516,"group"],[546,"group"],[561,"group"],[585,"group"],[603,"group"],[618,"group"],[636,"group"],[666,"group"],[690,"group"],[7235,"Group membership is managed by the reader. The old auto_join_consumer_group, poll_interval, batch_length and enum-based auto-commit consumer configuration are replaced by the current reader and PollOptions API."],[821,"Grouped fetches"],[6534,"Guide"],[6900,"Guide - client configuration reference and the full API surface: auth, streams, topics, partitions, publishing, consuming, offsets, consumer groups, system operations"],[1030,"Gzip"],[4209,"Half the open-file limit"],[3745,"Handle cross-origin requests with the rules below."],[3427,"Handle each response"],[225,"Handshake"],[4229,"handshake_grace"],[3913,"Hard ceiling on the write buffer. Writes past it error instead of buffering. Must exceed write_buffer_size by at least one message."],[4119,"Hard deadline for joining shard threads at exit. A wedged shard is abandoned with an error log. Must be at least shutdown_drain_timeout."],[3175,"Has no effect on client connections"],[3419,"Hash-based routing by key"],[2790,"Having in mind that stream consists of topics, which might have one or more partitions assigned, and each partition consists of segments, we can visualize the structure of the Iggy data directory as follows:"],[938,"Header kinds"],[229,"Header layouts"],[3025,"Header values don't have to be strings. They can also be numbers, booleans or raw bytes, so you can add things like a trace ID next to the type, as the typed-headers example shows. The message-compression example uses a header in the same way to record how the payload was compressed."],[5703,"headers"],[6198,"Headers and failure handling"],[113,"Health check"],[4585,"Heartbeat"],[6538,"Heartbeat"],[3093,"heartbeat