s on TCP"],[7249,"High-level vs low-level API"],[4595,"Highest throughput, lowest latency"],[2656,"Highly performant, persistent append-only log for message streaming"],[4625,"Historical benchmark comparison from the WebSocket implementation article (AWS i3en.3xlarge, 4 producers or consumers, 40M messages, 1,000 messages per batch, fsync enabled). These measurements predate 0.10.0:"],[3589,"Historical CLI screenshot. Server-start and cleanup flags shown there have been removed. Use the commands below and the current iggy-bench --help."],[3587,"Historical dashboard screenshot showing a 0.5.0 run, not 0.10.0 measurements."],[2655,"Historical startup screenshot from server 0.5.0. See configuration for the 0.10.0 settings."],[1166,"History identity captured with the request."],[5062,"HMAC-SHA256 validation uses the raw body, not reserialized JSON. Per-endpoint secrets belong in TOML or the management API. Local environment overrides target top-level plugin fields and do not populate nested endpoint secrets."],[3658,"Host and kernel settings are configured separately from the server TOML. See Linux tuning for service limits, memory policies, huge pages, CPU placement, and validation before deployment."],[4335,"Host kernel 5.19 or newer is required. Containers use the host's kernel, so these settings alone are not enough. See System requirements."],[4493,"Host settings affect both production latency and benchmark results. Start with the distribution defaults, satisfy Iggy's runtime requirements, then change one setting at a time. The examples below are experiments for dedicated Linux hosts, not a configuration to apply unchanged to every VM."],[6636,"Hostname"],[2744,"How a message flows through Iggy"],[2112,"How Apache Iggy replicates data across a cluster with VSR"],[2801,"How Apache Kafka's topics, partitions, consumer groups and offsets map to Apache Iggy, and what works differently."],[2312,"How configuration is resolved"],[3619,"How configuration loads"],[3577,"How