ed - you submit I/O requests to a submission queue (SQ), and the kernel completes them and places results in a completion queue (CQ). Both queues are shared ring buffers between user space and kernel. Submissions and completions can be batched to reduce syscalls. This is fundamentally better for disk I/O."],[4498,"io_uring_disabled=0 permits ring creation. With 1, an unprivileged service needs membership in the configured io_uring_group. With 2, creation is disabled. Container syscall filters can independently deny access. Configure access for the service rather than assuming that a root shell proves the container can start. See the kernel's io_uring controls and Docker deployment guidance."],[5674,"IoT / Sensor Relay (binary payloads)"],[1876,"ip"],[1954,"ip is not the bind interface for the client transports. tcp, quic, http, and websocket bind whatever their own address settings say. The roster supplies only their ports. The defaults bind loopback, so a cluster spread across hosts needs each transport's address set to 0.0.0.0 or the routable interface. The server warns at startup when a bind cannot serve the advertised ip."],[1997,"ip must be a literal IP address. Use advertised_address when clients can't reach it (see Configuration)"],[3770,"issuer"],[3772,"Issuer claim of minted tokens."],[3803,"issuer, audience, and jwks_url are required per entry. username names the active, non-root Iggy account to which the issuer maps. Provision that account before using its tokens. The old user_id key is rejected."],[3778,"Issuers accepted during validation."],[3498,"It is the only member, so it gets all three partitions and drains what the producer wrote:"],[6379,"It's also important to note, that the supported format(s) might vary depending on the connector implementation. For example, you might expect JSON as the payload format, which can be then easily parsed and processed by upstream components such as data transforms, but at the same time, you could support the other