d and committed progress while it catches up."],[2995,"Partition incarnation. The identity of one partition history. Deleting and recreating a partition changes it."],[2768,"Partition operations (send_messages, poll_messages, store_consumer_offset) are routed to the shard owning that partition via a lock-free concurrent map lookup. The request is sent into the owning shard's channel, whichever shard received it"],[6560,"Partition reader"],[2109,"Partition requests use the current partition route and can be forwarded in one hop to its primary. The contacted node signs the route and request with a relay proof. The destination rejects invalid or stale proofs and authenticates the caller separately. Proofs live for ten seconds, so synchronize node clocks. An uncertain result is returned without treating it as proof that a fresh replay is safe. ack=none confirms dispatch only."],[1852,"Partition requests use the partition route. It identifies the primary, view, partition incarnation and metadata progress. An incarnation identifies one history of a partition. Recreating a partition changes that identity. Consumer group operations also carry an ownership generation, so a former member cannot store progress for a new owner."],[819,"Partition routes"],[6720,"Partition selection is resolved client-side on both transports. Balanced partitioning round-robins over the topic's partitions, and key-based routing hashes the key with xxHash32 modulo the partition count, consistent with the Rust SDK for the same encoded key bytes and partition count. Strings use UTF-8, integers use little-endian bytes, and GUID keys use Guid.ToByteArray()."],[4151,"Partition storage and consensus tunables share this table. Unlike [metadata] (one plane on shard 0), a pipeline exists per partition, so raising per-partition budgets multiplies resource use by the partition count."],[2795,"Partition VSR replicates prepares. With durability=persisted, a multi-replica group requires recoverable prepare-WAL copies at the replication quorum before commit."],[1545,"partition_id"],[3414,"partition_id(n)"],[381,"partition_incarnation"],[441,"partition_incarnation"],[456,"partition_incarnation"],[471,"partition_incarnation"],[501,"partition_incarnation"],[528,"partition_incarnation"],[549,"partition_incarnation"],[564,"partition_incarnation"],[588,"partition_incarnation"],[606,"partition_incarnation"],[621,"partition_incarnation"],[651,"partition_incarnation"],[675,"partition_incarnation"],[699,"partition_incarnation"],[1164,"partition_incarnation"],[1377,"partition_incarnation"],[4108,"partition_io_bytes_max"],[4105,"partition_io_capacity"],[4911,"partition_resize_policy"],[2769,"Partition-to-shard assignment is deterministic: the packed IggyNamespace is hashed with Murmur3, and the upper 16 bits of the hash are taken modulo the shard count (the upper bits are used because Murmur3 has weak lower bits for small integer inputs)."],[2981,"Partition. Where a topic's messages are actually stored. A topic's messages are spread across its partitions. See Partition."],[3702,"partition.consumer_offset_enforce_fsync"],[3693,"partition.validate_checksum"],[3390,"PartitionClient - create, delete partitions"],[957,"PartitionId: kind = 2, length = 4, value is a u32 partition id."],[936,"Partitioning"],[3275,"Partitioning strategies"],[6556,"Partitioning strategies"],[2982,"Partitioning. How a producer picks the partition for a message: a fixed partition, round robin, or a hash of a message key. See Getting started."],[3491,"Partitioning.messages_key hashes the key to pick the partition, so orders for one customer share a partition and stay in order. The connection string comes from the environment, so the same script works against a server on another host (see Connection strings)."],[810,"Partitions"],[6553,"Partitions"],[3566,"Partitions - view partition details per topic"],[89,"Partitions & Segments"],[9,"Partitions distribute their primaries across cluster nodes. Topics can select the