hout writing them into the TOML file:"],[5388,"Top-level fields of plugin_config can be overridden (or injected) the same way with the IGGY_CONNECTORS_SOURCE_[KEY]_PLUGIN_CONFIG_[FIELD] pattern. This lets you supply credentials without writing them into the TOML file:"],[2363,"Top-level plugin_config fields can be overridden per connector via environment variables using the IGGY_CONNECTORS_{SINK|SOURCE}_{KEY}_PLUGIN_CONFIG_<FIELD> convention, e.g. IGGY_CONNECTORS_SINK_QUICKWIT_PLUGIN_CONFIG_URL."],[5040,"Top-level RFC3339 string field used to advance the watermark"],[1868,"Top-level settings"],[1660,"topic"],[2811,"Topic"],[2812,"Topic"],[2834,"Topic"],[2574,"Topic auto-creation is disabled by default. Enable IGGY_KAFKA_AUTO_CREATE_TOPICS_ENABLED only when Metadata requests are allowed to create missing topics. IGGY_KAFKA_AUTO_CREATE_TOPICS_PARTITIONS defaults to one and cannot exceed 1000."],[2576,"Topic configuration changes support retention.ms. The gateway is not a complete Kafka broker implementation. Unsupported API keys and most unsupported versions close the connection. ApiVersions has a discovery error response for unsupported versions. Use the protocol coverage for exact API version ranges."],[4372,"Topic option"],[4389,"Topic option"],[6552,"Topic options"],[4890,"Topic Options"],[7121,"Topic options: create_topic(..., options=TopicOptions(...)) accepts typed options. TopicOptions.raw accepts extra keys as dict[str, str], validated by the server. client.describe_options(\"topic\") lists the keys a server accepts."],[4673,"Topic permissions - scoped to one topic within a stream"],[4707,"Topic scope: manage_topic, read_topic, poll_messages, send_messages. read_topic includes poll_messages on that topic."],[3573,"Topic updates use the HTTP set/reset contract. Omitted fields keep their current values. See Topic options for mutable fields and creation-only policies. Some settings require the CLI or HTTP API."],[4542,"Topic usage and replica progress"],[4573,"t