use. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."],[5611,"Transforms can be applied before loading into Doris. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."],[5542,"Transforms can be applied before writing to Delta Lake. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."],[5886,"Transforms can be applied before writing to InfluxDB. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."],[6325,"Transforms can be applied before writing to S3. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."],[6491,"Transforms can be applied before writing to SurrealDB. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."],[2502,"Transforms mutate, filter, or convert messages as they flow through the connector runtime. They run inside the runtime process, not inside the plugins. For source connectors they're applied after the plugin's messages are decoded and before producing to Iggy. For sink connectors, after consuming from Iggy and before handing the messages to the plugin."],[2224,"Transforms run inside the runtime process, not inside the plugins. They are applied after decoding for sources (before sending to Iggy) and after consuming from Iggy for sinks (before forwarding to the external system)."],[2473,"Transforms: proto_convert supports JSON-to-protobuf schema encoding for scalar fields, including floating-point numbers and numeric enum values. Bytes and already-encoded nested messages use base64 strings. It logs and omits fields it cannot encode. Its protobuf-to-JSON path exposes Any metadata or raw-data metadata rather than decoding a custom message descriptor. Converting protobuf to flat_buffer or avro rewraps bytes without transcoding them."],[5732,"Transient errors (retried): network errors, HTTP 429, 500, 502, 503, 504."],[5731,"Transient failures allow up to max_retries additional attempts after the initial request: the default 3 means at most four attempts. Retry delays use full jitter from zero up to min(retry_delay * retry_backoff_multiplier^n, max_retry_delay), where n starts at zero for the first retry. With the defaults, the three delay caps are 1, 2 and 4 seconds."],[6125,"Transient insert failures are retried within the chunk. max_retries counts total attempts, and waits grow linearly as retry_delay, twice that delay, and so on. Retried SQLSTATEs are 40001, 40P01, 57P01, 57P02, 57P03, 08000, 08003 and 08006. SQLx I/O and pool-acquisition timeouts are also retried. Other errors stop that chunk's retry loop. Startup has no plugin retry loop."],[5949,"Transient submission and task-status errors are retried within their budgets. A failed indexing task is returned as an error without resubmitting it. A task timeout does not cancel the remote task, so it may finish later. The runtime records plugin errors and continues polling with consumer auto-commit. It does not replay failed batches. This does not provide an end-to-end at-least-once guarantee, and retries or manual replay after uncertain outcomes can repeat writes."],[4489,"Transparent huge pages"],[4510,"Transparent huge pages (THP)"],[15,"Transport"],[224,"Transport"],[1798,"Transport"],[3047,"Transport"],[3281,"Transport"],[3371,"Transport"],[4629,"Transport"],[4715,"Transport"],[4657,"Transport encryption (TLS)"],[4444,"transport is tcp, tcp_tls, ws, wss, quic or http. Binary connections keep their connection identity across reconnect retries. HTTP creates a new UUID for each login request."],[929,"Transport loss alone does not end a retained session. Logout, session expiry and account deactivation do. A password or PAT change does not revoke an already established session. Once the original session ends, unresolved operations cannot recover their old receipts through a new login."],[4577,"Transport protocols"],[3030,"Transport selection"],[3369,"Transport selection via scheme